---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import { SOCIAL } from "@/config/site-config";

const effectiveDate = { iso: "2026-10-22", label: "October 22, 2026" };
---

<Layout
	title="SPS Privacy Policy"
	ogImage="images/social-preview.png"
	description="How the Self Prompting System (SPS) Discord application is intended to handle data.">
	<article>
		<section class="mb-10">
			<p class="text-xs text-neutral-content mb-2">
				<span class="text-success font-bold">$</span>
				<span class="ml-1 text-warning">cat ~/sps/PRIVACY</span>
				<span class="blink" aria-hidden="true">_</span>
			</p>
			<h2><i class="icon-shield-check"></i> SPS Privacy Policy</h2>
			<p>
				This policy covers the <b>Self Prompting System</b> ("SPS") Discord application, a private engineering tool I operate.
				It is separate from this website. The <a href="/privacy/">website privacy policy</a> covers alexmbugua.me and its
				guestbook, and none of the guestbook's storage, spam filtering, or vendor arrangements apply to SPS.
			</p>
			<p>
				Effective <time datetime={effectiveDate.iso}>{effectiveDate.label}</time>. Read it alongside the <a
					href="/sps/terms/">SPS Terms of Service</a
				>.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mb-10">
			<p class="text-xs text-neutral-content mb-2">
				<span class="text-success font-bold">$</span>
				<span class="ml-1 text-warning">sps status</span>
				<span class="blink" aria-hidden="true">_</span>
			</p>
			<h2><i class="icon-hourglass-split"></i> Where things stand</h2>
			<p>
				SPS is a Windows-first orchestration system that runs locally and carries out engineering work through Claude
				Code and Codex CLI workflows, using my existing sign-ins to those tools. A supervised fixture controller exists
				today.
			</p>
			<p>
				<b>The Discord application is planned and not yet operational.</b> It does not collect anything from Discord at the
				moment. This page describes how it is intended to handle data, published ahead of launch. It is not a sign that Discord
				collection is already active.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mb-10">
			<p class="text-xs text-neutral-content mb-2">
				<span class="text-success font-bold">$</span>
				<span class="ml-1 text-warning">sps help</span>
				<span class="blink" aria-hidden="true">_</span>
			</p>
			<h2><i class="icon-discord"></i> What the Discord interface is for</h2>
			<p>
				It is meant for operators I have explicitly authorized, not for the public. Through slash commands, buttons, and
				forms, it is intended to:
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>show progress on authorized runs</li>
				<li>receive feedback</li>
				<li>control authorized runs, such as pausing and resuming them</li>
				<li>collect explicit operator decisions, such as reviewing delivery candidates</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="mb-10">
			<p class="text-xs text-neutral-content mb-2">
				<span class="text-success font-bold">$</span>
				<span class="ml-1 text-warning">sps schema --records</span>
				<span class="blink" aria-hidden="true">_</span>
			</p>
			<h2><i class="icon-database"></i> What SPS is intended to record</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<b>Discord identifiers:</b> your user ID, and the server, channel, and interaction IDs for each interaction.
				</li>
				<li>
					<b>What you submit:</b> the text you enter in commands and forms, including feedback. This is content you write,
					and it is recorded as submitted.
				</li>
				<li><b>Timestamps</b> for interactions and the actions they trigger.</li>
				<li
					><b>Action dispositions and operator decisions</b>, such as whether a run was paused or a candidate approved.</li
				>
				<li><b>References to engineering evidence</b> and audit records associated with a run.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Please keep passwords, tokens, and other people's personal information out of anything you submit. I can't
				promise that submitted feedback, evidence, or exports will never contain sensitive information, so the safest
				approach is not to put it there.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mb-10">
			<p class="text-xs text-neutral-content mb-2">
				<span class="text-success font-bold">$</span>
				<span class="ml-1 text-warning">sps schema --exclude</span>
				<span class="blink" aria-hidden="true">_</span>
			</p>
			<h2><i class="icon-circle-slash"></i> What it is not meant to collect</h2>
			<p>
				General conversation in Discord servers is outside what SPS is intended to collect. The initial design does not
				automatically ingest arbitrary channel messages or uploaded attachments. It works with what you deliberately
				send it through its commands, buttons, and forms.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mb-10">
			<p class="text-xs text-neutral-content mb-2">
				<span class="text-success font-bold">$</span>
				<span class="ml-1 text-warning">sps trace --data-flow</span>
				<span class="blink" aria-hidden="true">_</span>
			</p>
			<h2><i class="icon-diagram-3"></i> Where data goes</h2>
			<p>Not all of it stays on one machine:</p>
			<ul>
				<li><b>My computer:</b> controller state is stored on my Windows computer, where SPS runs.</li>
				<li>
					<b>Model providers:</b> selected feedback and task context may be passed to <b>Anthropic</b> (through Claude Code)
					or{" "}
					<b>OpenAI</b> (through Codex) to carry out the work. Once sent, it is handled under that provider's own terms and
					privacy policy.
				</li>
				<li>
					<b>Discord:</b> every interaction passes through Discord. Status summaries and selected evidence may be posted to
					the configured Discord channel, where anyone who can view that channel can read them.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="mb-10">
			<p class="text-xs text-neutral-content mb-2">
				<span class="text-success font-bold">$</span>
				<span class="ml-1 text-warning">sps where --state</span>
				<span class="blink" aria-hidden="true">_</span>
			</p>
			<h2><i class="icon-hdd"></i> Storage</h2>
			<p>
				The current fixture controller keeps its state in a SQLite database, along with artifact and evidence files, on
				my Windows computer, outside the project's source repository.
			</p>
			<p>
				The storage protections that will apply to Discord data are still being settled. They will be described here
				before Discord collection begins.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mb-10">
			<p class="text-xs text-neutral-content mb-2">
				<span class="text-success font-bold">$</span>
				<span class="ml-1 text-warning">sps retention --show</span>
				<span class="blink" aria-hidden="true">_</span>
			</p>
			<h2><i class="icon-clock-history"></i> Retention</h2>
			<p>
				There is no fixed retention period, and nothing deletes records automatically yet. Records are kept because they
				support running work, recovering from interruptions, and keeping an audit history. I review them and remove them
				when they're no longer needed. That review is a commitment I carry out by hand, not an automated mechanism.
			</p>
			<p>
				Before Discord collection is switched on, I will settle retention periods, deletion procedures, and storage
				protections, and update this policy to match.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mb-10">
			<p class="text-xs text-neutral-content mb-2">
				<span class="text-success font-bold">$</span>
				<span class="ml-1 text-warning">mail -s "SPS request" {SOCIAL.email}</span>
				<span class="blink" aria-hidden="true">_</span>
			</p>
			<h2><i class="icon-envelope-at"></i> Access, correction, and deletion</h2>
			<p>
				To ask for a copy of SPS records about you, or to have them corrected or deleted, email me at <a
					href={`mailto:${SOCIAL.email}`}>{SOCIAL.email}</a
				>. Include your Discord username or user ID, and roughly when and where the interaction happened (server,
				channel, approximate date). Never send passwords, tokens, or other credentials. You don't need to open a public
				issue for this.
			</p>
			<p>
				I can review and remove records SPS stores locally and, once the Discord interface is active, messages the bot
				has posted to Discord. Copies held by Discord, Anthropic, or OpenAI are subject to their own controls and
				policies, so removing something from my records may not remove it from theirs.
			</p>
			<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-4">
				<a href={`mailto:${SOCIAL.email}`} class="link-action no-underline">
					<i class="icon-envelope-at"></i>
					{SOCIAL.email}
				</a>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="mb-10">
			<p class="text-xs text-neutral-content mb-2">
				<span class="text-success font-bold">$</span>
				<span class="ml-1 text-warning">ls ~/sps/third-party/</span>
				<span class="blink" aria-hidden="true">_</span>
			</p>
			<h2><i class="icon-link-45deg"></i> Third-party privacy information</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<a href="https://discord.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Discord Privacy Policy</a>
				</li>
				<li>
					<a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>Anthropic Privacy Policy</a
					>
				</li>
				<li>
					<a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/data-usage" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>Claude Code data usage</a
					>
				</li>
				<li>
					<a href="https://openai.com/policies/privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>OpenAI Privacy Policy</a
					>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="mb-10">
			<p class="text-xs text-neutral-content mb-2">
				<span class="text-success font-bold">$</span>
				<span class="ml-1 text-warning">git log -- ~/sps/PRIVACY</span>
				<span class="blink" aria-hidden="true">_</span>
			</p>
			<h2><i class="icon-calendar-event"></i> Changes</h2>
			<p>
				Material changes will be reflected on this page with an updated date. Once the Discord interface is active,
				authorized operators will also get a notice when this policy changes.
			</p>
			<p>Last updated <time datetime={effectiveDate.iso}>{effectiveDate.label}</time>.</p>
		</section>

		<hr class="my-8 border-base-300" />

		<section class="mb-6">
			<p class="text-xs text-neutral-content mb-2">
				<span class="text-error font-bold">$</span>
				<span class="ml-1 text-warning">exit</span>
				<span class="blink" aria-hidden="true">_</span>
			</p>
			<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-4">
				<a href="/sps/terms/" class="link-action no-underline">
					<i class="icon-file-earmark-text"></i>
					SPS Terms
				</a>
				<a href="/privacy/" class="link-action no-underline">
					<i class="icon-shield-check"></i>
					Website Privacy
				</a>
			</div>
		</section>
	</article>
</Layout>
